      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! The wiki has a direct answer to your question.\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **credential scoping**:\n\n1. **The key is never loaded into the Hub\u0027s environment**: A local secrets loader reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n\n2. **The key is injected only into child processes**: The key is injected directly into the environment of spawned child processes (the Ingest agent or Query agent) immediately before those processes start.\n\n3. **The Hub\u0027s process environment is never mutated**: The Hub\u0027s own process environment remains unchanged and never contains the credential.\n\nThe security benefit is clear: even if the Hub process were compromised or misbehaving, it could not leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 4316,
      "output_tokens": 214
    }
